 "tutorial": [
  "# 1. THE TERMINAL",
  "You work in the terminal. Type a command and press ENTER. TAB completes, UP/DOWN browse history.",
  "# 2. THE LOOP",
  "  scan  inspect a server     connect <host>  open a connection",
  "  firewall  breach defences  login <user>  authenticate",
  "  ls / cd / cat  explore     download  take what you need",
  "# 3. TRACE ALERT",
  "Every mistake raises the TRACE ALERT bar. At 100% you are burned and the mission fails. Disconnecting cools it down fast.",
  "# 4. MISSIONS",
  "'mission' shows your objectives, 'missions' lists every operation by chapter. Bonus goals pay extra.",
  "# 5. THE MARKET",
  "'market' sells tools, upgrades, themes, access and intel. Better reputation = cheaper prices.",
  "# 6. LOADOUT",
  "'loadout' shows five gear slots (TRACE, DECRYPT, FIREWALL, NETWORK, UTILITY). 'equip <id>' boosts your stats.",
  "# 7. DAILY & WEEKLY",
  "'daily claim' and 'weekly claim' pay credits, XP and rare items. Come back every day for the streak.",
  "# 8. HIDDEN THINGS",
  "'ls -a' reveals hidden files. Some commands and servers are secret. ZERO leaves hints.",
  "# 9. EVERYTHING IS A SIMULATION",
  "All servers, IPs and files exist only inside NEXUS. Nothing real is ever touched.",
  "Shortcuts: ESC pause · F5 quick save · F11 fullscreen · Ctrl+L clear"
 ]
